    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0243" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Woodrow Wilson Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of Labor</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-27">27 November,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Thank you for sending me
                        Walsh’s letter about Mr. Gompers. Mr. Gompers needs no commendation,
                    so far as I am concerned, but I am entirely of your opinion about the
                    representation, or the apparent representation, of special classes or
                    interests.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow
                                Wilson</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
